Boot screen: rebuild only the K114s kernels' images on the K114s.

Local change for this machine, not an upstream fix. omarchy-plymouth-set (behind the "boot screen
matches theme" action, omarchy-plymouth-set-by-theme) runs a bare `sudo limine-mkinitcpio`, which
rebuilds the image of every installed kernel. On this Mac that includes the held stock
linux-aurora, whose image docs/esp-space.md keeps off the EFI partition: on 2026-11-24 one boot
screen change put its 79 MB image back, added a third menu entry, left 43 MB free and stopped the
next update at the space guard.

Where /proc/device-tree/compatible lists apple,k114s, the rebuild names the installed
linux-k114s* kernel packages instead, through limine-mkinitcpio only (never mkinitcpio -P), one
kernel at a time. Before each one it checks that the EFI partition is mounted and has the space
guard's minimum free (one new image is written beside the old one), and otherwise refuses with
the command to run later. Other machines are unchanged.

Paths are relative to /usr.

--- a/bin/omarchy-plymouth-set
+++ b/bin/omarchy-plymouth-set
@@ -373,7 +373,33 @@
 if [[ $mode != "refresh-sddm" ]]; then
   sudo plymouth-set-default-theme omarchy
 
-  if omarchy-cmd-present limine-mkinitcpio; then
+  # K114s local change: a bare limine-mkinitcpio rebuilds the image of every installed kernel,
+  # including the held stock linux-aurora, whose 79 MB image fills the EFI partition, adds a third
+  # boot menu entry and stops every later update (docs/esp-space.md). On the K114s only the
+  # linux-k114s* kernels' images are rebuilt, through Limine only, one kernel at a time, each only
+  # when the mounted EFI partition has room for one image beside the old one.
+  if grep -qx 'apple,k114s' < <(tr '\0' '\n' 2>/dev/null <"${K114S_DT_COMPATIBLE:-/proc/device-tree/compatible}"); then
+    k114s_kernels=($({ pacman -Qqo /usr/lib/modules/*/modules.builtin 2>/dev/null || true; } | sort -u | sed -n -E '/^linux-k114s(-|$)/p'))
+    if ! omarchy-cmd-present limine-mkinitcpio; then
+      echo "limine-mkinitcpio is missing; the boot images were not rebuilt (mkinitcpio -P is not used on this Mac)." >&2
+      exit 1
+    elif (( ${#k114s_kernels[@]} == 0 )); then
+      echo "No linux-k114s kernel is installed; the boot images were not rebuilt." >&2
+      exit 1
+    fi
+    for k114s_kernel in "${k114s_kernels[@]}"; do
+      k114s_free=
+      if mountpoint -q /boot/efi; then
+        k114s_free=$(df -B1 --output=avail /boot/efi 2>/dev/null | tail -n 1 | tr -d ' ') || k114s_free=
+      fi
+      if [[ ! $k114s_free =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || (( k114s_free < ${K114S_ESP_MIN_FREE:-88080384} )); then
+        echo "The EFI partition is not mounted, unreadable or too full to rebuild the $k114s_kernel image beside the old one." >&2
+        echo "The boot screen changes at the next rebuild; once there is room: sudo limine-mkinitcpio ${k114s_kernels[*]}" >&2
+        exit 1
+      fi
+      sudo limine-mkinitcpio "$k114s_kernel"
+    done
+  elif omarchy-cmd-present limine-mkinitcpio; then
     sudo limine-mkinitcpio
   else
     sudo mkinitcpio -P
